---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import LoadCurve from '../components/LoadCurve.astro';
import NextChapter from '../components/NextChapter.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { image } from '../images';
import { url } from '../site';
---

<Base title="Atlanta Energyshed" active="">
  <header class="page-head wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Chapter 1 of 5</p>
    <h1 class="hero__title">Where Atlanta's electricity comes from, and where it could go</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Atlanta's <strong>energyshed</strong> is every source of electricity that powers the region's homes, businesses
      and transit: rooftop solar, distant power plants, and the wires that tie them together across several states.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="curve-label">
    <p class="card-label" id="curve-label">A summer day on the grid</p>
    <LoadCurve />
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap">
    <div class="split split--figure-wide">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Supply and demand</h2>
        <p>
          Like most dense urban areas, metro Atlanta is a consumption island. Its demand is met by a supply network
          that stretches far beyond city limits, with power plants, transmission lines and fuel sources spread across
          multiple states.
        </p>
        <p>
          That's why the region's energy resilience, prices and environmental footprint only make sense in this
          broader context.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <Figure src="supply_area.png" alt="Map of the balancing authority area that balances electricity supply and demand for the region" caption="The balancing authority that matches supply to demand" />
        <Figure src="demand_area.png" alt="Map highlighting the high-demand metro Atlanta area" caption="The high-demand metro Atlanta area" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap">
    <div class="split split--figure-wide split--reverse">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>How power reaches you</h2>
        <p>
          Electricity flows from high-voltage generation and transmission lines through a spiderweb of distribution
          lines to your outlet. Each step along the way loses a little more power.
        </p>
        <p>
          Large customers take on more of that system themselves. Substation customers, such as Electric Membership
          Corporations, and primary customers, such as large factories, maintain their own distribution equipment.
          Homes and small buildings get end-to-end service, including upkeep and repairs, from the utility. That's
          one reason different customers pay under different pricing models.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Figure src="grid_structure.png" alt="Diagram of the power grid from generation and transmission through substations to primary and secondary customers" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap">
    <div class="split split--text-wide">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>How it's changing</h2>
        <p>
          The region is at a turning point. Population growth and new development are making energy needs more
          complex, while new technology is changing both how much power we use and where it comes from.
        </p>
        <p>
          Energy-hungry data centers are arriving fast. Grid equipment is ageing. Existing homes and offices need
          retrofits to use energy well. Managing peak demand and electrifying buildings are both a challenge and an
          opportunity for a more resilient system.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Figure src="defining_atlanta_how_changing.png" alt="Illustration of the forces changing Atlanta's energy system" max={380} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap">
    <h2 class="levers__title">Three levers this tool explores</h2>
    <ul class="levers">
      <li>
        <a href={url('efficiency/')}>
          <Image src={image('defining_energy_efficiency.png')} alt="" widths={[360, 560, 840]} sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 300px, 100vw" format="webp" quality={82} />
          <h3>Energy efficiency</h3>
        </a>
        <p>
          Heat pumps can cut heating and cooling energy by up to half. Better insulation, air sealing and windows stop
          waste and make homes more comfortable.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={url('local-generation/')}>
          <Image src={image('defining_local_gen_storage.png')} alt="" widths={[360, 560, 840]} sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 300px, 100vw" format="webp" quality={82} />
          <h3>Local generation and storage</h3>
        </a>
        <p>
          Rooftop solar makes clean power on site. Batteries save it for the evening or an outage, and electric
          vehicles with two-way charging can do the same.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={url('grid/')}>
          <Image src={image('defining_grid.png')} alt="" widths={[360, 560, 840]} sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 300px, 100vw" format="webp" quality={82} />
          <h3>The grid itself</h3>
        </a>
        <p>
          Instead of one-way delivery from big plants, the grid now has to handle power flowing both ways from solar,
          batteries and vehicles, while data centers add new load.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <NextChapter slug="" />
</Base>

<style>
  .hero__title { max-width: 22ch; font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 4.4vw, 3.1rem); line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -0.03em; }

  .pair { display: grid; gap: 20px; grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr; align-items: start; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .pair { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  .levers__title { margin-top: 0; }
  .levers li { border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); padding: 14px; background: var(--paper-sunken); }
  .levers {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1.2rem 0 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 16px;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
  }
  .levers a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; display: block; }
  .levers img {
    background: #fff;
    border-radius: 6px;
    border: 0;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    object-fit: contain;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 10px;
  }
  .levers h3 { margin: 0.9rem 0 0.4rem; }
  .levers a:hover h3 { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 0.18em; }
  .levers p { color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0; }
</style>
